From: Andrea Mattera <26578395+m0s4ik@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: reset the queue pointer in prepare

Not upstream: carried by thinksmart-view-debian (driver/q6asm), on top of
222d04cf55bc ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: wrap the position of a full ring
to 0"). Found by reading the code, not yet confirmed on hardware.

q6asm_dai_ack() queues to the DSP every whole period between queue_ptr
and appl_ptr. After a prepare ALSA sets appl_ptr back to 0, while
queue_ptr keeps the value it reached in the previous run. The
difference is computed as unsigned long and stored in an int: it
wraps, and once divided by the period size and truncated it is
negative or huge depending on the period size. With 480, 2400 or 4800
frames per period it is negative and nothing is queued any more: the
stream stalls in silence. With 960, 1440 or 1920 frames it is between
about 0.5 and 1.1 billion, and the loop sends bogus WRITE_V2 commands
under the stream lock until the transport refuses one.

Until 222d04cf55bc an underrun was never detected, because the
position stopped one frame short of appl_ptr, so few applications
re-prepared a playback stream. Since that commit an underrun is
detected and recovered with a prepare, so this is hit on every xrun
recovery, as well as after snd_pcm_drop() followed by a prepare.

Reset queue_ptr where prepare succeeds, next to the state change:
ALSA only resets appl_ptr after a successful prepare. Doing it on the
STOP trigger would not be enough, because a stream can be dropped from
PREPARED, with periods already queued, without a STOP trigger.

This is the q6asm-dai counterpart of cab45ab95ce7 for q6apm-dai.

Fixes: e386c2cf3df2 ("ASoC: qcom: q6asm-dai: schedule all available frames to avoid dsp under-runs")
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c | 7 +++++--
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6asm-dai.c
@@ -294,10 +294,13 @@
 			q6asm_read(prtd->audio_client, prtd->stream_id);
 
 	}
-	if (ret < 0)
+	if (ret < 0) {
 		dev_info(dev, "%s: CMD Format block failed\n", __func__);
-	else
+	} else {
+		/* ALSA restarts appl_ptr from 0 after a prepare */
+		prtd->queue_ptr = 0;
 		prtd->state = Q6ASM_STREAM_RUNNING;
+	}
 
 	return ret;
 
